'''''Populus laurifolia''''', the '''laurel poplar''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Salicaceae]], native to Kazakhstan, the [[Altai Mountains|Altai]], Mongolia, and [[Xinjiang]] in China.<ref name="776748-1" >{{cite web |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:776748-1 |title=''Populus laurifolia'' Ledeb. |author=<!--Not stated--> |website=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Board of Trustees of the Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew |access-date=26 October 2021 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=''Populus laurifolia'' laurel poplar |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/88349/i-populus-laurifolia-i/details |date=2021 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=26 October 2021 }}</ref> It hybridizes readily with other species of poplar, and has high genetic variation.<ref>{{cite journal |title=When exotic poplars and native ''Populus balsamifera'' L. Meet on the Canadian Prairies: Spontaneous hybridization and establishment of interspecific hybrids |year=2012 |last1=Talbot |first1=Patricia |last2=Schroeder |first2=William R. |last3=Bousquet |first3=Jean |last4=Isabel |first4=Nathalie |journal=Forest Ecology and Management |volume=285 |pages=142–152 |doi=10.1016/j.foreco.2012.07.036 }}</ref>

